,"repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T15:51:43Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T15:51:43Z","body":"His question is, why not implement multiscattering with this all in one go instead of after this gets merged.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2810013619/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2810335172","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103934#issuecomment-2810335172","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103934","id":2810335172,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ngk_E","user":{"login":"LiveTrower","id":48926464,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4OTI2NDY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48926464?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower","html_url":"https://github.com/LiveTrower","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T18:07:21Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T18:17:58Z","body":"> His question is, why not implement multiscattering with this all in one go instead of after this gets merged.\r\n\r\nOkay, that's clearer. The reason was that I wanted to keep the PR simple since it's my first PR, and I wasn't sure if this approach was appropriate because I didn’t know if you'd agree with the time it takes for Godot to generate the DFG LUT, and thus make more changes.\r\n\r\nMy plan was as follows:\r\n\r\n- Create this first PR, where the current approximation is replaced by the LUT, and get it approved and merged.\r\n- Continue with the second PR, where multiscattering would be applied with a new specular mode called MultiscatteringGGX. This is because multiscattering is only noticeable on metallic materials with high roughness, while there’s no visual difference in non-metallic materials.\r\n\r\n- The final PR would be sheen shading (but that will be more complicated to implement in Godot’s current state due to multiple issues in the GLSL code for applying lighting). Someone has already been making fixes in [#100681](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100681), [#100348](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100348), [#100503](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100503), and [#100383](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100383), but unfortunately, there’s no further news on that.\r\n\r\nThese are the main issues:\r\n1. Like clear coat, sheen shading has to scale diffuse and specular by (1.0 - max3(sheen_color) * dfg_sheen * sheen).\r\n2. Clear coat doesn’t take reflection probe reflections into account, so sheen shading would suffer from the same problem.\r\n3. The IBL of the clear coat is not correct since a BRDF approximation is not applied and in the case of sheen shading its own BRDF must also be applied.\r\n\r\nFixing these issues would also involve solving the clear coat problems, so I’d rather wait for proper solutions to make it easier to fully implement sheen shading later.\r\n\r\nSo, if you prefer, I can combine the first two PRs into one, but the third one will remain in limbo.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2810335172/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2810570392","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103934#issuecomment-2810570392","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103934","id":2810570392,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nheaY","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T19:35:17Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T19:35:17Z","body":"I'd say merging the first two PRs into one makes sense.\r\n\r\nAs far as the blocker PRs mentioned go for sheen shading, I don't know what their statuses are... If they need more work or are in the massive PR review backlog (seems like the latter at a glance)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2810570392/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2810617269","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103934#issuecomment-2810617269","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103934","id":2810617269,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nhp21","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T19:56:15Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T19:56:15Z","body":"> I'd say merging the first two PRs into one makes sense.\r\n\r\nAgreed. For context, we discussed this in the rendering meeting today and the consensus was that it looks slightly better (presumably more accurate which is good), but was really very noticeable. Given that we should move to a multiscattering model anyway, we figured it would make more sense to do both together. \r\n\r\n> As far as the blocker PRs mentioned go for sheen shading, I don't know what their statuses are... If they need more work or are in the massive PR review backlog (seems like the latter at a glance)\r\n\r\nThey need more work. What they need is someone willing to champion the PRs and help the contributor get them into a mergable state (i.e. improve code quality, test, ensure compatibility is maintained). I helped on the other big overhaul PRs, but I don't have the bandwidth right now to provide that much assistance. \r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2810617269/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2815819027","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103934#issuecomment-2815819027","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103934","id":2815819027,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n1f0T","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-18T16:37:48Z","updated_at":"2025-04-18T16:37:48Z","body":"Note that there's no need to squash until this has been approved and is ready to merge","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2815819027/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2844643775","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103934#issuecomment-2844643775","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103934","id":2844643775,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pjdG_","user":{"login":"Ansraer","id":6329420,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjk0MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6329420?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer","html_url":"https://github.com/Ansraer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-01T10:58:05Z","updated_at":"2025-05-01T10:58:16Z","body":"> However, the SPECULAR_GGX constant should be renamed back to SPECULAR_SCHLICK_GGX as this breaks compatibility otherwise. While the Schlick GGX name will be technically incorrect when using Forward+, we favor keeping compatibility with existing projects as much as possible.\r\n\r\n@Calinou Why? Isn't the numerical value used for serialization? If so, how would changing the string name change anything?\r\n\r\nhttps://chat.godotengine.org/channel/general/thread/29LjmAoEafWQ8Xwri","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2844643775/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2845266316","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103934#issuecomment-2845266316","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103934","id":2845266316,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pl1GM","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-01T17:06:19Z","updated_at":"2025-05-01T17:06:19Z","body":"> > However, the SPECULAR_GGX constant should be renamed back to SPECULAR_SCHLICK_GGX as this breaks compatibility otherwise. While the Schlick GGX name will be technically incorrect when using Forward+, we favor keeping compatibility with existing projects as much as possible.\r\n> \r\n> @Calinou Why? Isn't the numerical value used for serialization? If so, how would changing the string name change anything?\r\n> \r\n> https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/general/thread/29LjmAoEafWQ8Xwri\r\n\r\nIn GDScript if I have a line of code that uses `SPECULAR_SCHLICK_GGX` I would get a parse error with this PR. Using the GDExtension system we can indeed handle compatibility for extensions and TSCN's will also work fine. But there is no reason to break user scripts for an arbitrary name change. API changes should only happen when they are needed","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2845266316/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2861482950","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103934#issuecomment-2861482950","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103934","id":2861482950,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qjsPG","user":{"login":"LiveTrower","id":48926464,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4OTI2NDY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48926464?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower","html_url":"https://github.com/LiveTrower","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-08T03:04:57Z","updated_at":"2025-05-08T03:04:57Z","body":"> Code looks good to me.\r\n> \r\n> Please squash the commits together into a single commit. See [PR workflow](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/community/contributing/pr_workflow.html#mastering-the-pr-workflow-the-rebase) for instructions 🙂\r\n\r\nDone.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2861482950/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2867180308","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103934#issuecomment-2867180308","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103934","id":2867180308,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6q5bMU","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"h